## Solution 1: Fix the SCORM Content

If you have access to the SCORM package source:

### Look For:
```javascript
// BAD - Only showing percentage
document.getElementById('score').innerHTML = '13%';

// GOOD - Setting SCORM API
API.SetValue('cmi.core.score.raw', '13');
API.SetValue('cmi.core.score.max', '100');
```

### What It Should Do:
```javascript
// CORRECT SCORM 1.2 implementation
var correct = 13;
var total = 100;

// Set in SCORM API
API.SetValue('cmi.core.score.raw', correct.toString());
API.SetValue('cmi.core.score.max', total.toString());

// ALSO display to user (optional)
document.getElementById('score').innerHTML = correct + '/' + total + ' (' + ((correct/total)*100).toFixed(1) + '%)';
```

