## Solution 2: Use the Fallback Handler

If you can't modify the SCORM content, use the fallback solution that tries multiple score extraction methods:

**Replace your `finalizeWithScore` function with the one in `SCORM_FALLBACK_FIX.js`**

This fallback:
1. ✅ Tries fraction format first (13/100)
2. ✅ Falls back to SCORM API (cmi.score.raw, cmi.score.max)
3. ✅ Falls back to inner frame API calls
4. ✅ Finally uses percentage if nothing else works

